---
/*
  /work/legacy-renovations - case detail (Legacy Kitchen & Bathroom Renovations).
  Data-only; layout + CSS live in the shared CaseStudy component. Copy drafted for
  Alex's morning review (runbook A2/C3); the Tony R. quote is real (positioning §10,
  low-signal friend-client, usable as proof). Hero uses the real legacy-renovations
  screenshot; live-site link is on hand. See .impeccable/surfaces/src-pages-work.md.
*/
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CaseStudy from "../../components/CaseStudy.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Legacy Renovations · Work · Proudly Sites"
  description="How a Raleigh kitchen and bathroom renovation company got its first real brand and a site that leads with the finished work."
>
  <CaseStudy
    niche="Kitchen & Bath"
    location="Raleigh"
    title="Craftsmanship homeowners can see before they call"
    liveUrl="https://www.legacykitchenbathroomrenovations.com"
    heroImage="/images/legacy-renovations.jpeg"
    heroAlt="A finished Legacy Renovations kitchen remodel leading the site"
    who="A kitchen and bathroom renovation company in the Raleigh area, building its first real brand."
    whatChanged="A site that leads with finished work, so homeowners can see the craftsmanship before they ever pick up the phone."
    moment={[
      "Homeowners do not hire a remodeler the way they buy most things. They are handing someone the keys to their house, so they hire the person they trust, usually the one a neighbor or a friend already vouched for. Legacy had the referrals and the finished work to back them up.",
      "What they did not have was a place to send those referrals that did the work justice. This was their first real brand, and the site had to do two things at once: look like the quality of the renovations, and make requesting a quote feel like the obvious next step.",
    ]}
    built={[
      "The build leads with the finished work. Photographs of completed kitchens and baths carry the page, and the brand stays quiet on purpose, so the craftsmanship is what you notice first.",
      "Service pages are organized the way homeowners actually search, with the search foundations to match, so the right people find Legacy in the first place. Every project photo can be added by the owner, not a developer, so the portfolio stays as current as the work does, and requesting a quote is never more than a click away.",
    ]}
    changed={[
      "The site now runs smoothly and looks like the work. Legacy can send any referral to a page that confirms exactly what they were told, and add every new project themselves the day it is finished.",
    ]}
    quote={{
      text: "“The design looks amazing, the site runs smoothly, and everything was completed on time.”",
      cite: "Tony R., Legacy Renovations",
    }}
    next={{ label: "Strictly Clean Detailing", href: "/work/strictly-clean-detailing" }}
  />
</BaseLayout>
